@page "/legal/cookies"
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Cookies · GymStation</PageTitle>

<main class="legal-shell">
    <header>
        <a class="legal-home" href="/">GYMSTATION</a>
        <h1>COOKIES</h1>
        <p class="legal-date">EFFECTIVE 2026-08-02</p>
    </header>

    <p>
        GymStation sets two cookies. Both are strictly necessary for the site to work,
        which is why there is no cookie banner — there is nothing to opt in or out of.
    </p>

    <h2>THE FULL LIST</h2>
    <p><b>.AspNetCore.Identity.Application</b> — keeps you signed in. Created when you
        sign in, removed when you sign out.</p>
    <p><b>.AspNetCore.Antiforgery.*</b> — protects every form on the site from
        cross-site request forgery (the name ends in a framework-generated suffix).
        Set automatically; contains no personal information.</p>

    <h2>WHAT WE DON'T SET</h2>
    <p>No analytics cookies, no advertising cookies, no third-party cookies of any kind.
        Your theme preference is stored on your account, not in a cookie, so it follows
        you between devices.</p>

    <p class="legal-note">If you block these cookies in your browser, signing in and
        submitting forms will not work.</p>

    <PlatformFooter />
</main>
